# A1 — Deep Expert Audit Shortcut

When the user types **`A1`** (or "run A1"), perform this task:

> Do a complete, deep, expert-level analysis and audit of the project across ALL
> parameters. Check whether it is **production-ready** and **enterprise-ready**,
> and give it a numeric rating.

## Scope

- Project: `pdf-doctor` (OnlyMyPDF).
- **Do NOT modify the conversion pipeline** (merge/compress/pdf-to-word engines,
  LibreOffice/Puppeteer/pdf-lib services, `pdf-to-word.service.ts`, conversion scripts).
- Read-only audit: gather evidence from code, run typecheck/tests if useful, but
  do not change app behavior unless the user explicitly asks.

## Parameters to score (each /100)

Cybersecurity, Privacy/GDPR, Auth/Access control, Billing/Payments,
Enterprise/B2B, DevOps/CI-CD, Observability/Ops, Scalability, Testing/Quality,
Code quality, SEO, AEO, Accessibility (a11y), Performance, i18n, Legal/UX copy.

## Output format

1. **Overall score /100** + grade (A/B/C/D/F) + one-line verdict.
2. **Scorecard table** — parameter, score, grade, 1-line reason.
3. **Strengths** (bullets).
4. **Gaps / risks** (bullets, prioritized P1/P2/P3).
5. **Production-ready?** and **Enterprise-ready?** — clear yes / yes-with-conditions / no, with the blocking conditions.
6. **Top next actions** (short, ordered).

Keep it evidence-based (cite files/routes), concise, and honest — no inflated scores.
